    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0330" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123W85/171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi><anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d187-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-13T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mission’s 5478, November 29, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>For Wood. You are assigned to Mr. Dresel’s mission. Upon his departure for Berlin
                    you may in his discretion proceed Munich unofficially and temporarily for
                    observation purposes. You should not however establish consular office.</p>
                <p>Same for Stewart changing Munich to Hamburg.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d187-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d187-f1" n="13" type="source" xml:id="d187-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Embassy at Paris as No. 9331.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d187-f2" n="14" xml:id="d187-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 3876, Nov. 24, 3 p.m., to the Commission, the suggestion that
                    Consul Sauer be stationed at Cologne was approved (File No. 123W85/168).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
